Chinese 给/給 and fused recipient phrases are the main cues. Preceding
transfer verbs weaken the response. Vietnamese cho/cấp, Thai ให้ and Korean
급 are other cues; their split-token spellings are handled explicitly.
There is also a separate positive response to a document-opening 'Title:'.
Unrecognized tokens receive zero, not a claim that all synonyms behave alike.
