String-opening punctuation gives a negative response; primes and Rust lifetime
marks give a positive one. A quote after a space depends on the preceding word
or punctuation and on nearby programming syntax. Other tokens give zero,
apart from a document-start offset and a response to paired middle dots.
The amplitudes are conservative averages, not word-specific lookups.
