"""layers.1.mlp.down_proj:3566, a "this is where the text announces what comes next" unit.

It is near zero almost everywhere. It switches on at the point where the writer is about to
state, list, or conclude something:
  * a colon that opens an explanation or list: "...the following:", "is:", "Note:", "as follows:",
    "Example:", and the same colon at the end of a line (":\n", ":\n\n"), which is strongest;
  * a line break right after a section heading such as "Summary", "Conclusions", "Discussion";
  * a comma closing an opener like "In summary,", "From the results,", "According to ...,";
  * reporting verbs that lead into a finding: "showed", "seems", "suggest", "we see/know that",
    "can be seen", and the Chinese "来看/看/来说/显示" ("judging from", "shows").
